An **open circle** marks a boundary that is **not** included, used for $<$ and $>$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\usetikzlibrary{arrows.meta}
\draw[{Stealth}-{Stealth}] (-2.9,0)--(2.9,0);
\node[right] at (3,0) {$x$};
\draw (0,0.12)--(0,-0.12);
\node[below] at (0,-0.18) {$a$};
\draw[very thick,-{Stealth}] (0,0)--(2.35,0);
\draw[fill=white] (0,0) circle (2.4pt);
\node at (-1.6,0.6) {$x>a$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A **closed circle** marks a boundary that **is** included, used for $\le$ and $\ge$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\usetikzlibrary{arrows.meta}
\draw[{Stealth}-{Stealth}] (-2.9,0)--(2.9,0);
\node[right] at (3,0) {$x$};
\draw (0,0.12)--(0,-0.12);
\node[below] at (0,-0.18) {$a$};
\draw[very thick,-{Stealth}] (0,0)--(2.35,0);
\fill (0,0) circle (2.4pt);
\node at (-1.6,0.6) {$x\ge a$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Shade **right** towards larger values for $>$ and $\ge$, and **left** towards smaller values for $<$ and $\le$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\usetikzlibrary{arrows.meta}
\draw[{Stealth}-{Stealth}] (-2.9,0)--(2.9,0);
\node[right] at (3,0) {$x$};
\draw (0,0.12)--(0,-0.12);
\node[below] at (0,-0.18) {$a$};
\draw[very thick,-{Stealth}] (0,0)--(-2.35,0);
\draw[fill=white] (0,0) circle (2.4pt);
\node at (1.6,0.6) {$x<a$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A between inequality such as $-1<x\le3$ is drawn as a segment with a circle at each end, one open and one closed here.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\usetikzlibrary{arrows.meta}
\draw[{Stealth}-{Stealth}] (-2.9,0)--(2.9,0);
\node[right] at (3,0) {$x$};
\draw (-1.2,0.12)--(-1.2,-0.12);
\node[below] at (-1.2,-0.18) {$a$};
\draw (1.2,0.12)--(1.2,-0.12);
\node[below] at (1.2,-0.18) {$b$};
\draw[very thick] (-1.2,0)--(1.2,0);
\draw[fill=white] (-1.2,0) circle (2.4pt);
\fill (1.2,0) circle (2.4pt);
\node at (0,0.6) {$a<x\le b$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

