One number line shows $x>-2$ and another shows $x\le3$.
On the number line below, show the values that satisfy **both**, then write the single inequality.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}
\draw[{Stealth}-{Stealth}] (-2.9,0)--(2.9,0);
\foreach \v in {-5,...,5} {\draw (0.5*\v,0.12)--(0.5*\v,-0.12); \node[below] at (0.5*\v,-0.16) {$\v$};}
\node[right] at (3,0) {$x$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

mastery.solution_text:
A value must be larger than $-2$ and also no larger than $3$, so only the values between the boundaries work.
$-2$ is excluded, so its circle is open; $3$ is included, so its circle is closed.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}
\draw[{Stealth}-{Stealth}] (-2.9,0)--(2.9,0);
\foreach \v in {-5,...,5} {\draw (0.5*\v,0.12)--(0.5*\v,-0.12); \node[below] at (0.5*\v,-0.16) {$\v$};}
\draw[very thick] (-1,0)--(1.5,0);
\draw[fill=white] (-1,0) circle (2.4pt);
\fill (1.5,0) circle (2.4pt);
\node[right] at (3,0) {$x$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
$-2<x\le3$

$1\le x$ says $1$ is less than or equal to $x$, so $x\ge1$: a closed circle at $1$ with the arrow to the right.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}
\draw[{Stealth}-{Stealth}] (-2.9,0)--(2.9,0);
\foreach \v in {-5,...,5} {\draw (0.5*\v,0.12)--(0.5*\v,-0.12); \node[below] at (0.5*\v,-0.16) {$\v$};}
\draw[very thick,-{Stealth}] (0.5,0)--(2.7,0);
\fill (0.5,0) circle (2.4pt);
\node[right] at (3,0) {$x$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
$x\le1$ keeps the closed circle at $1$ but shades the smaller values instead.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}
\draw[{Stealth}-{Stealth}] (-2.9,0)--(2.9,0);
\foreach \v in {-5,...,5} {\draw (0.5*\v,0.12)--(0.5*\v,-0.12); \node[below] at (0.5*\v,-0.16) {$\v$};}
\draw[very thick,-{Stealth}] (0.5,0)--(-2.7,0);
\fill (0.5,0) circle (2.4pt);
\node[right] at (3,0) {$x$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
The only value the two solution sets share is $1$; every other number belongs to exactly one of them.
